== To You!

#smallcaps[The] aim of this book is the salvation of the reader. The one who spoke and wrote it will be bitterly disappointed if it does not lead many to the Lord Jesus. It is sent out in childlike dependence on the power of God the Holy Spirit, to use it in the conversion of millions, if he pleases. No doubt many poor men and women will pick up this little book, and the Lord will visit them with grace. With them in mind, the plainest language has been chosen, and many everyday expressions have been used. But if the wealthy and well-placed should glance at this book, the Holy Spirit can reach #emph[them] too; for what the uneducated can understand is no less appealing to the educated. Oh, that some who read it might become great winners of souls!

Who knows how many will find their way to peace through what they read here? A more important question for you, dear reader, is this — #emph[Will you be one of them]?

A certain man placed a fountain by the wayside, and he hung up a cup next to it on a little chain. Some time later he was told that a great art critic had found much fault with its design. “But,” he said, “do many thirsty people drink at it?” Then they told him that thousands of poor people, men, women, and children, quenched their thirst at this fountain; and he smiled and said that the critic’s remark did not trouble him much, only he hoped that on some hot summer’s day the critic himself might fill the cup, and be refreshed, and praise the name of the Lord.

Here is my fountain, and here is my cup: find fault if you like; but #emph[do drink the water of life]. This is all I care about. I would rather bless the soul of the poorest street sweeper or rag collector than please a royal prince and fail to convert him to God.

Reader, do you mean business in reading these pages? If so, we are agreed from the start; but nothing short of your finding Christ and heaven is what this book aims at. Oh, that we may seek this together! I do so by dedicating this little book in prayer. Will you not join me by looking up to God and asking him to bless you while you read? Providence has put these pages in your way, you have a little spare time in which to read them, and you feel willing to give them your attention. These are good signs. Who knows? Perhaps the time God has set for blessing you has come. At any rate, “The Holy Spirit says, ‘Today, if you#super[+] hear His voice, do not harden your hearts.’”
